🚀 DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 1

Linux Fundamentals (0–2 Years Experience)

If you want to become a DevOps Engineer, Linux is non-negotiable.
Almost everything in DevOps — servers, containers, Kubernetes nodes, CI/CD agents — runs on Linux.

📌 Devops Tool 1 Focus: Core Linux Interview Questions

• What is Linux and why is it widely used in DevOps?
• Difference between Linux and Unix
• What is a shell? Difference between bash and sh
• Explain Linux directory structure (/etc, /var, /opt, /usr)
• What is root user? How is it different from normal user?
• File permissions (r, w, x) and chmod explained
• Difference between chmod 755 and chmod 777
• What is umask?
• Hard link vs soft link
• How do you check running processes?
• Difference between ps, top, and htop
• How do you kill a process in Linux?
• What is a daemon process?
• How do you check disk usage and memory uses 
• Difference between df and du
• What is a package manager? (yum, apt)
• How do you find a file in Linux?
• What is grep and why is it important?
• What is SSH and how does it work?
• How do you check Linux logs?

💡 Interview Tip:
Most beginners fail DevOps interviews not because of cloud or tools — but because of weak Linux fundamentals.
